# The corpus list is deliberately not published. See README.md, "Ethics".
# Owner/name exists only in .env. Nothing that describes a subject more
# precisely than the README's banded table may be committed:
#
#   .env                 owner/name, pinned SHAs, precise ratios
#   t2.local.json        real T2 task text (quotes in-repo file paths)
#   T2-tasks.md          internal task design notes (same reason)
#   corpus-manifest.json per-repo file/byte histograms (a verification oracle)
#   runs/                per-run records; final responses quote the tree
#   repositories/, work/, probe/, runs/logs/   local artefacts
#
# Published artefacts are the harness, the method, and the banded aggregate
# tables. Anything not listed above is public.
.env
runs/
t2.local.json
T2-tasks.md
corpus-manifest.json
ground-truth/
reports/*.local.*
repositories/
work/
probe/
*.log
__pycache__/
.ruff_cache/
.cavet/
.run.lock
*.err
